  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of MgCu₃ (Mg₄Cu₁₂ per cell) crystallizes in the tetragonal space group I-4m2 (No. 119), with 16 atoms in the unit cell distributed over four independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-only CrystalNN analysis identifies close-packed-like local arrangements for both Cu and Mg: each Cu center has 12 geometric neighbors (10 Cu, 2 Mg), while each Mg center has 12 Cu neighbors, with neighbor distances ranging from about 2.63 to 2.78 Å. The geometric neighbor graph forms a single three-dimensional component spanning all 16 sites. Validated polyhedron-sharing analysis reveals Cu–Cu 12-vertex polyhedra exhibiting corner, edge, and face sharing, and Cu–Mg polyhedra sharing corners and edges.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
